# Git conventions (next-dato)

Always write **commit messages** and **PR titles** as [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). English, imperative, one line subject.

```
type(scope): description
```

Release Please ([`.github/workflows/release.yml`](../../.github/workflows/release.yml)) groups the CHANGELOG by **type**; **scope** is how Next.js vs DatoCMS work is categorized (`feat(cms):`, `fix(next):`).

## Types

`feat` · `fix` · `docs` · `chore` · `refactor` · `perf` · `ci` · `test`

## Scopes (required when it fits)

| Scope | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `cms` | Dato models, CDA queries, blocks, draft/preview |
| `ui` | Components, layout, Tailwind |
| `seo` | metadata, JSON-LD, sitemap, robots |
| `deps` | dependency bumps |
| `core` | `src/core/` entities / use-cases |
| `next` | App Router, `next.config`, cache, proxy |
| `codegen` | GraphQL codegen / generated types |

## DatoCMS breaking schema

Removing/renaming CDA fields or required GraphQL shapes:

```
feat(cms)!: drop ImageBlock.assetDesktop

feat(cms): require captions on video_block

BREAKING CHANGE: video_block.captions is now required in PAGE_BY_SLUG.
```

`!` after the type/scope **or** a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer → major bump (Release Please).

## PRs

- Title = same Conventional subject as the main commit.
- Body = [`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`](../../.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md).

```
# ✅
feat(cms): add FAQ group Structured Text block
fix(next): skip fetch cache in draft mode
chore(codegen): regenerate operations after PAGE_BY_SLUG

# ❌
Updated stuff
Ajustes no Dato
feat: new block
```
